      "text": "Let the integer be $x$. We want to find the value of $x$ such that $x^2 < 2x$.\n\nRearranging the inequality, we have $x^2 - 2x < 0$.\n\nFactoring out an $x$, we have $x(x-2) < 0$.\n\nTo find the values of $x$ that satisfy this inequality, we can use a sign chart:\n\n\\begin{center}\n\\begin{tikzpicture}\n\\draw[->] (-3,0) -- (5,0) node[right] {$x$};\n\\draw[->] (0,-1) -- (0,3) node[above] {$y$};\n\\draw[thick] (0,0) -- (2,0) node[right] {$x=0$};\n\\draw[thick] (2,0) -- (3,0) node[right] {$x=1$};\n\\draw[thick] (3,0) -- (4,0) node[right] {$x=2$};\n\\draw[thick] (4,0) -- (5,0) node[right] {$x=3$};\n\\draw[thick] (0,-1) -- (0,0) node[below] {$y=-1$};\n\\draw[thick] (0,0) -- (0,1) node[below] {$y=0$};\n\\draw[thick] (0,1) -- (0,2) node[below] {$y=1$};\n\\draw[thick] (0,2) -- (0,3) node[below] {$y=2$};\n\\draw[thick] (0,3) -- (0,3) node[below] {$y=3$};\n\\draw[thick] (0,0) -- (0,3) node[below] {$y=3$};\n\\draw[thick] (0,3) -- (0,3) node[below] {$y=3$};\n\\draw[thick] (0,3) -- (0,3) node[below] {$y=3$};\n\\end{tikzpicture}\n\\end{center}\n\nFrom the sign chart, we see that the inequality $x(x-2) < 0$ holds for $0 < x < 2$.\n\nSince we are looking for an integer solution, the only possible value for $x$ is $\\boxed{1}$.",
